OL,3,GNEWSACan someone display my 450-ship
OL,4,Amatchstick model navy?
OL,5,
OL,6,FA master model maker, who has spent 78
OL,7,Fyears making matchstick navy ships, is
OL,8,Fappealing for a museum to take on his
OL,9,Fcollection as he prepares to retire.
OL,11,FPhillip Warren, from Blandford, Dorset,
OL,12,Fis hoping his matchstick armada can go
OL,13,Fon show to the public.
OL,15,FThe 96-year-old, who stopped making the
OL,16,Fwarships a few years ago, was 17 when
OL,17,Fhe started the hobby in 1948.
OL,19,FHe has made 544 model ships in total
OL,20,Fbut his current collection stands at
OL,21,F450.
